  "interpretation": "## What changed\n\nUse grew across every measure in the latest 14 days. Users increased by 13.27 percent, times started by 17.57 percent, and actions by 43.02 percent.\n\nActions grew faster than users, which suggests that people are doing more with Excel MCP after they start using it.\n\n## How well it worked\n\nMost actions finished without reporting an error. Reading and writing cells finished without an error 99.57 percent of the time.\n\nFinding cells had the most room to improve, finishing without an error 97.06 percent of the time. Opening workbooks, running macros, checking refreshed data, and taking screenshots sometimes took much longer than usual.\n\n## How people use it\n\nReading and writing cells made up 39.35 percent of all actions. Opening and closing workbooks made up another 18.03 percent.\n\nRelease 1.10.5 handled the most actions. Release 2.0.2 was used by 87 users during the latest period.\n\n## What we will improve\n\nWe will investigate failures when finding cells and look for ways to make opening workbooks faster.\n\nWe will keep starts separate from real work so brief availability checks do not look like active use.\n\nWe will continue improving the quality of the background problem reports shown on this page.",
